# 14. DETERMINE REAL PROJECT PROGRESS

Never derive progress merely from:

- commit count
- file count
- issue count
- README checklist

Progress means:

> how close the component is to reliably performing its intended production responsibility.

Use:

```text
✅ READY
🟢 MOSTLY READY
🟡 PARTIAL
🟠 BLOCKED
🔴 BROKEN
⚪ NOT STARTED
❓ UNKNOWN
```

---

# 15. PROGRESS MODEL

Evaluate at least:

```text
IMPLEMENTATION
BUILD
RUNTIME
CONFIGURATION
DATABASE
INTEGRATION
TESTING
CI/CD
OBSERVABILITY
DOCUMENTATION
DEPLOYMENT
```

Only use percentages when enough evidence exists.

---

# 16. UMBRELLA PROGRESS

Do NOT calculate:

```text
closed_issues / total_issues
```

Instead consider weighted deployment capability:

- Build Readiness
- Runtime Readiness
- Database Readiness
- Integration Readiness
- Core Functionality
- CI/CD Readiness
- Deployment Readiness
- Production Validation

Use approximate progress, not false precision.

